INT. REGIONAL SOCK WAREHOUSE - RETURNS CAGE - DAY

KWABENA OSEI-BONSU (40s, lanyard, three pens) glares at a pallet of mismatched socks. BRENDA TUCKWELL (50s, headset) and her intern PRIYA NAIR (20s, hoodie) hover.

                    KWABENA
          Every single one is a left foot.

                    BRENDA
          Socks don't have feet.

                    KWABENA
          Brenda, this is the Q3 initiative.

                    PRIYA
          The initiative was "pairing synergy."

                    KWABENA
          And she wrote the memo. She also approved the vendor. She also, apparently, ordered only lefts.

                    BRENDA
          I approved a vendor. He ordered the lefts.

                    PRIYA
          So he's the problem, then? He shipped what she approved.

                    KWABENA
          Priya, he did not write the memo, she did.

                    BRENDA
          He rewrote my memo, actually. I wrote "pairs."

                    PRIYA
          He wrote "pair." Singular. One pair of socks.

                    KWABENA
          Fine. Fine. Then we ship one pair to every customer and call it exclusive.

                    BRENDA
          I'll put that in the deck.

                    PRIYA
          I'll put it in the apology.
